      "stability": "evolving",
      "version_field": "Runtime.protocol_version",
      "notes": "Runtime protocol owns canonical request, response, event, report, proof, and system envelopes. Version 2 removes the implicit permission and hook control channel. Participant lifecycle events use one nested common participant record with disjoint live, completed, and failed payloads; legacy flat payloads are rejected."
